          "modelAnswer": "Domain adaptation (transductive transfer):\n• Same task in the source and target, but the data distribution / domain differs (e.g. sentiment on movie reviews → sentiment on product reviews, or news → tweets).\n• Data: labelled data in the source domain, while the target domain has little or no labelled data (often only unlabelled target data).\n• Goal: make a model trained on the source distribution work on the shifted target distribution.\n\nSequential transfer learning (inductive transfer):\n• Different tasks, learned one after the other: first pretrain on a source task, then adapt (fine-tune) to the target task.\n• Data: a huge, general, usually unlabelled corpus for pretraining (e.g. Wikipedia/web text with a language-modelling objective, as in ELMo, BERT and GPT), then a smaller labelled, task-specific dataset for the target task.\n• Goal: reuse general knowledge of language for a new task.",
