          "question": "What is weight tying in a neural language model, and what is its trade-off? (2 Marks)",
          "modelAnswer": "Weight tying uses the same matrix for the input word embeddings and the output word embeddings (the final layer that scores every token). It roughly halves those (very large) parameter matrices. The trade-off is less flexibility: one vector per word has to serve both for reading the word and for predicting it.",
